ce:section.ce:para:
In this study, MABet was synthesized by the esterification reaction between -OH groups of betulin at C3 and C28 positions and maleic anhydride (
                           Fig. 1 A inset). Betulin (2.6 g, 6.0 mmol), maleic anhydride (3.0 g, 30 mmol), and dichloromethane (100 mL) were added into a 250 mL round-bottom flask and magnetically stirred for 30 min (500 r/min). Afterwards, TEA (4.2 mL) was added dropwise. After being reacted at 25 ℃ for 24 h, the obtained mixture was washed three times with 2% HCl and deionized water and dried over anhydrous MgSO4. The organic phase was collected via filtration and then concentrated using rotary rotavapor to achieve a light-yellow solid (3.2 g, 83.6% yield; 
                           Fig. 2B). 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3, Fig. 1a): δ (ppm) = 6.49 (dd, J = 12.8, 5.7 Hz, 2 H), 6.40 (dd, J = 16.8, 12.8 Hz, 2 H), 4.73 (d, J = 2.2 Hz, 1 H), 4.71–4.65 (m, 1 H), 4.64 (q, J = 2.7, 2.2 Hz, 1 H), 4.52 (ddd, J = 8.6, 6.8, 1.9 Hz, 1 H), 4.06 (dd, J = 11.0, 1.4 Hz, 1 H), 2.46 (dq, J = 11.0, 5.8 Hz, 1 H), 2.00–0.75 (multiple peaks, the pentacyclic triterpene skeleton of betulin). 13C NMR (151 MHz, CDCl3, Fig. 1b): δ (ppm) = 167.95, 167.62, 165.26, 164.93, 149.66, 136.21, 135.62, 129.81, 129.47, 110.23, 84.78, 65.57, 55.32, 50.21, 48.79, 47.67, 46.40, 42.73, 40.88, 38.28, 37.92, 37.69, 37.05, 34.38, 34.03, 29.52, 29.40, 27.96, 26.95, 25.06, 23.35, 20.78, 19.11, 18.11, 16.45, 16.16, 16.05, 14.77. FTIR (Fig. 1c): υ (cm−1) = 3443 (O-H), 1711 (CO), 1164 (C-O). HR-MS (TOF MS ES-, DCM, Fig. 1d): calculated C38H54O8 for 638.3819 m/z; observed 637.3741 m/z [M-H]-.
